						<td class="title">
							Tiran's Bio
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							Tiran Wren sits down upon the soft grass beneath the willow and begins his meditation. He will not be disturbed here. He often comes to this spot, seldom frequented by others, when he needs to think. The glade is quiet and very peaceful and Tiran can hear the sound of the waterfall not far away.<br />
<br />
He contemplates his life in the face of the events of the day. His future is as uncertain as his past... his life simply a steady movement forward through the darkness. The stranger had hissed a name at him, a name he didn't recognize. That name, he marvels, may very well have changed the course of his life. The power of such a simple word.<br />
<br />
Tiran wanted nothing of it. NOTHING!<br />
<br />
Tiran.<br />
<br />
&quot;Tiran,&quot; he thinks almost out loud, his lips moving as the word coalesces in his mind. As good a name as any. He does not know or care for the other.<br />
<br />
Tiran closes his eyes and concentrates on his breathing. Very slowly, he becomes transparent. His body evaporates and expands outward from himself. It becomes the tree, the grass, the water, the sunlight. He expands himself further, feeling the life around him merge and become one. People pass through him. Wars rage within and around him. He is a part of everything.<br />
<br />
How simple everything seems now. All life is connected; everything a part of everything else. Death and life the very same thing.<br />
<br />
Tiran comes back into himself. He has decided: he will move forward. There is no other direction to go; no other path to follow. His past is his past. If it chases him, so be it. He will meet it again in the future if it wishes to confront him.<br />
<br />
He lies back and closes his eyes. It is not late, but he is very tired and must sleep for a time. He concentrates and then smiles to himself as a new face comes into view.							&nbsp;
